  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Study for socio-economic benefits of Nature-Based solutions (NbS) for coastal protection on the Petit Cote, Senegal</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This activity supports a study assessing the socio economic impacts of applying Nature-based Solutions for coastal protection along the Petite C&#xf4;te near Dakar (Mbao, Yarakh, Yenne). The study examines how NbS can help protect livelihoods such as fisheries, tourism, housing and small businesses while reducing climate risks for coastal communities.With a focus on benefits for youth and women, the study analyses local socio-economic dependencies, identifies opportunities for community involvement in NbS maintenance and evaluates broader development benefits. The assessment is based on desk research, engagement with local institutions and field interviews.</narrative>
  </description>
